content.text:
Loop: add input.update and victory delay. Where? After FPS block, before state branch. But `input.update` reads pad and adds look. We call `readLook` in playing/dead branch, but in menu no consumption. look accumulates; on startGame, camYaw may get old accumulated gamepad look. Minor. Could call readLook only playing/dead. In menu, look accumulates if gamepad connected; startGame doesn't clear look. Add `this.input.lookX=0; this.input.lookY=0;` in startGame? or call consumeLook in menu. Simplest: call input.update at top; for non-playing states, discard look? Could do at top:
```
this.input.update(dt);
if (this.state !== 'playing' && this.state !== 'dead') this.input.consumeLook();
```
But update in menu and paused is okay. Also gamepad pressed pause edges accumulate; global hotkey only plays. On resume pressed cleared. fine.

Victory delay: after state branch and poll? Best in playing branch after pollActions:
```
if (this.victoryDelay > 0) {
  this.victoryDelay -= dt;
  if (this.victoryDelay <= 0) this.showVictory();
  }
```
But showVictory changes state mid-loop, still effects etc run after; already in playing branch, then common effects etc below. It will run once. Fine. Could place after the if/else state branch before common; but `showVictory` sets state; effects common still runs for current frame. okay.

Let's edit.

